# Open Data

Never fetch Open Data from the browser (CORS, rate limits, cache). Use `lib/opendata/client.ts` on the server.

- Paris: `opendata.paris.fr` (`host` omitted or `"paris"`).
- Montreuil: `data.montreuil.fr` (`host: "montreuil"`).
- Explore v2.1 `limit` max is 100. Paginate with `fetchAllRecords` and a stable `orderBy` when `idField` is a scalar.
- New datasets: add a `DatasetConfig` in `lib/opendata/datasets.ts`, then a page. Do not hardcode dataset ids in UI.
- District filters live on `DatasetConfig.district`, not a switch on dataset id. Vélib’ uses station-code prefixes, not `nom_arrondissement_communes = 'Paris'`.
- Prefer a scalar or composite text `idField` (`arrondissement,adresse`). Do not use a geo object as the favorite id.
- Large geo sets (`bbox: true`, e.g. trees, chantiers, dans-ma-rue): bbox queries only, never dump the full catalog.
- `/api/opendata/records` is session-only, bbox datasets only. Rebuild district filters on the server; never accept client `where`.
- React list/map keys must be unique strings. Use `recordId()`, never `String(geoObject)` (`"[object Object]"`). Append `::${index}` when ids can collide.
- Maps: Leaflet via `components/map/dynamic-map.tsx` (`ssr: false`).
- Prefer `fetchRecordsSafe` / `fetchCount` on dashboards so one dead API does not crash the page.
- `fetchRecordsSafe` / `fetchAllRecords` return `{ ok, page, error }`. Show `DatasetNotice` when `ok` is false; do not treat a failed fetch as an empty city.
- Landing / overview Vélib’ KPIs use `fetchAggregate` (`sum(...)`), never `fetchAllRecords` of the full catalog.
